      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://zip9.kr/post/2026%EB%85%84-%EC%8B%A0%ED%98%BC%EB%B6%80%EB%B6%80-%ED%8A%B9%EB%B3%84%EA%B3%B5%EA%B8%89-%EC%86%8C%EB%93%9D-%EC%9A%94%EA%B1%B4-%EC%99%84%ED%99%94-%EB%B6%84%EC%84%9D-%EB%B0%8F-%EC%B2%AD%EC%95%BD-%EB%A7%9E%EC%B6%A4%ED%98%95-%EC%9E%90%EA%B8%88-%EC%A1%B0%EB%8B%AC-%ED%94%8C%EB%9E%9C-%EA%B0%80%EC%9D%B4%EB%93%9C</guid>
      <description>                                      *    21                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          &apos;            No                                      O                2                                                                      2                G.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    *                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    *                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              * Single switch unit selection up, center, and down  -      **The main switch board is at the center top. It holds basic  operations for whole of the software.  **  -  `Select layout`:  **Selects the initial view structure.** User can select the  one of the default    layouts.  -  `Lock/Unlock`:  **Enable/Disable the custom layout modification.**  User cannot change the position, size, addition/removal of widget if  the panel is locked.  -  `Reset`:  **Resets the current layout** to its default settings, which can  be useful if the layout of panels becomes chaotic.  -  `Save`:  **Saves the workspace&apos;s state**, like selected features, active  filters, color settings etc. and customized layouts.  -  `Export`:  **Export/download data/images** of currently active panel in multiple  formats like JSON, CSV, PDF, PNG, SVG etc.  -  `Full Screen`:  Toggle full screen of the browser.  -  `Configuration`:  **Global configuration.** Includes background theme selection, changing    the font family for all text components in the board.  -  `Add Panel`:  **Add more panels to the layout.** We currently support 14    built-in widgets (Chart, Map, KPI, Text, Image etc. )  -  `Help`:  Open up a side drawer with short tutorials and  reference.  -  `User Profile`:  Modify user settings, check subscription status etc.  -  `Search`:  Perform keyword search through all columns of current dataset.  -  `Reset filters`:  Reset all filters applied via the chart, map or filter widgets.  -  `Total Records`:  Displays total rows of active dataset being used.  -  `Query duration`:  Displays the time elapsed for querying the active dataset.  ***  ####  **`b. Panel Title`**  The user has the option to display the panel title at the top of the card. This is configurable within each panel&apos;s local settings.  ####  **`c. Chart / Widget Plotting Area`**  This is the primary container for the visual representations of your data (e.g., bar, line, pie chart).  ####  **`d. Panel Footer / Pagination`**  An optional section at the bottom of the card. It typically displays pagination controls, particularly for Table and Pivot Table panels.  ####  **`e. Local Panel settings`**  The settings panel on the right sidebar. When a user clicks &apos;edit&apos; on a specific panel, this drawer opens. It contains all the tools to customize that specific panel&apos;s data, appearance, and behavior, which are divided into different tabs:  -  `DATA`:  For selecting, filtering, and organizing the data to be  presented.  -  `VISUAL`:  For customizing the appearance of the chart (colors, axis  labels, legend, etc.).  -  `INTERACTIONS`: For defining how the panel interacts with other panels (e.g., cross-filtering, drill-down).  -  `DESIGN`:  For fine-tuning style details like border, background, and  padding.  ***  ## 2. Grid System and Layout  #### **`A` Grid Layout**  The workspace uses a `12-column grid` system. All panels (widgets) can be resized and repositioned on this grid.  ####  **`B` Responsive Design**  When designing a dashboard, it&apos;s essential to consider how it will look on different screen sizes (Desktop, Tablet, Mobile). The grid system. automatically wraps and scales panels to fit the screen.  -  **Desktop**: 12 columns.  -  **Tablet**: 6 columns.  -  **Mobile**: 2 columns.  -  We use `react-grid-layout` under the hood.   -  Whenever we can we use standard `Tailwind CSS` for styling the dashboard&apos;s elements.  ---  ## 3. Creating and Managing Panels  To build a dashboard, users add and configure panels:  1. **Add Panel**: Click the **Add Panel** (➕) button in the Header.  2. **Select Type**: Choose from the available panel types (e.g., Bar, Line, Table, KPI).  3. **Configure Data**:  - Select a **dataset** (or use the workspace default).  - Map your data fields to the **X-axis**, **Y-axis**, **Group By**, etc.  4. **Style the Panel**: Use the **VISUAL** &amp; **DESIGN** tabs to customize colors, labels, and borders.  5. **Set up Interactions**: Use the **INTERACTIONS** tab to enable cross-filtering with other panels.  ---  ## 4. State Management (The </description>
